request.description:
Stream the answer token-by-token using Server-Sent Events. The first token arrives in ~1 s. Best option for WP plugins — shows text progressively instead of waiting for the full response.

Each line in the response stream is a JSON event prefixed with 'data: ':

- Token chunk:  data: {"token": "The "}
- Cache hit:    data: {"answer": "...", "sources": [...], "done": true, "from_cache": true}
- Stream done:  data: {"done": true, "sources": ["doc-1"]}
- Error:        data: {"error": "PLAN_LIMIT_REACHED", "done": true}

Note: Postman shows the raw SSE stream in the response body. Use browser DevTools or a custom client to see tokens arrive in real time.

